AB  - The emergence of vehicular networks integrated with Artificial Intelligence (AI) technologies has created new promising opportunities for intelligent transportation systems. One of the newly adapted AI techniques is Generative Artificial Intelligence (GenAI), which provides significant capabilities in addressing numerous challenges in vehicular networks. We review the challenges associated with vehicular networks and explore how GenAI models can solve them. The specific challenges that we focus on include efficient data communication, enhanced network security, and intelligent data management for driving applications, as well as data generation and augmentation for rare and complex driving scenarios. Moreover, we discuss future research directions, such as adopting federated learning, 6G-enabled communications, synthetic data generation for rare events, intelligent resource management, and secure vehicular communications. We hope that the results of this work will provide a useful reference for researchers planning to leverage GenAI technology in developing intelligent, secure, and data-efficient vehicular networks.
