KW  - Federated learning
KW  - Differential privacy
KW  - Adaptive mechanism
KW  - Scale-aware
KW  - Collusion attack defense
AB  - The application of Federated Learning (FL) in data-sensitive domains faces severe privacy challenges due to its dynamic and open nature. Existing differential privacy (DP) schemes, which rely on static noise mechanisms, struggle to adapt to the fluctuations in participant scale caused by frequent client join/leave events. This leads to a dilemma between wasted privacy budget and degraded utility, coupled with a lack of effective defense against collusion attacks. This paper proposes AdaScaleDP, a scale-aware differential privacy aggregation scheme designed for dynamic FL. Its core innovations are threefold: (1) We propose a dynamic sensitivity model that, for the first time, formally establishes a power-law relationship between the statistical sensitivity and the actual participant scale, providing a theoretical foundation for adaptive noise; (2) We design an adaptive noise generation mechanism that dynamically adjusts the noise intensity according to the participant scale, achieving optimal privacy budget allocation; (3) We introduce a dynamic noise dilution defense paradigm, which transforms the privacy protection mechanism into an active defense weapon by coupling noise with scale, effectively mitigating collusion attacks. Formal proofs demonstrate that our scheme satisfies (ϵ,δ)-DP even in strong adversarial settings where the proportion of malicious clients is below 50% and that of malicious servers is below 33%. Large-scale experiments show that, compared to state-of-the-art schemes, AdaScaleDP reduces the aggregation error by 9.84% on average. This improvement is particularly pronounced for scale-sensitive normalized statistics (e.g. MEAN and VARIANCE), with error reduction reaching up to 14.85% and 23.48%, respectively, under various adversarial settings. For linear statistics (e.g. SUM, MAX), consistent but more modest gains (3%–6% in benign settings) are observed. Furthermore, AdaScaleDP increases the defense success rate against collusion attacks by 28%, while incurring only 5.6% additional computational overhead. This research provides a reliable solution that synergistically optimizes privacy, utility, and security for open federated learning environments.
ER  - 

