KW  - Temporal semantic modeling
KW  - Cross-modal fusion
AB  - The Internet of Vehicles (IoV) enables interaction among intelligent connected vehicles through multi-modal data, such as sensors, communication networks, video feeds, and text logs. However, expanding external interfaces and transmission flaws have intensified security risks. Attacks now exhibit diversified and cross-domain characteristics, posing significant safety challenges. Critically, most existing studies focus solely on single-modal data. As a result, they struggle to mitigate comprehensive attacks involving multi-modal heterogeneous information. Furthermore, traditional methods often lack robust temporal modeling capabilities. They fail to capture the spatio-temporal correlations required to identify covert threats. Leveraging large model technology, this review systematically categorizes IoV multi-modal data types and analyzes core technical requirements for intrusion detection. It specifically investigates research progress in temporal semantic modeling, cross-modal fusion, and adversarial defense. The specific advantages and challenges of these models in enhancing detection accuracy are also evaluated. The paper concludes by summarizing current research limitations. Future directions are then proposed, including dynamic adaptive systems, 6G collaborative security, and quantum-inspired defense, to guide theoretical and practical advancements.
ER  - 

