AB  - This chapter provides an in-depth overview of four major attack types targeting AI data: data poisoning, privacy attacks, data extraction, and data tampering and forgery. It details the mechanisms and characteristics of poisoning attacks, explores privacy leakage through various inference techniques, and explains how data extraction can reconstruct original training data from models. The chapter also distinguishes between ordinary tampering and deepfake, particularly in facial image manipulation. As the use and complexity of AI systems grow, the risks of data misuse and privacy violations intensify, underscoring the urgent need for continued advancement in defense technologies to safeguard sensitive information.
