AB  - This study constructs a privacy infrastructure vulnerability detection and automated processing architecture based on multimodal artificial intelligence technology. This study considers the security risks faced by multimodal AI systems as a comprehensive optimization problem. While maintaining the operational stability of the model, it strives to improve the efficiency of vulnerability discovery and remediation. It defines metrics related to attack surface assessment, vulnerability detection, and defense costs. This paper conducts an in-depth discussion of the application of multimodal AI models in privacy protection. Based on experimental analysis and data mining, this study meticulously verifies the effectiveness and practicality of the framework in practical operations. Compared with traditional methods, the framework demonstrates higher levels of detection accuracy. The framework’s robustness and adaptability are enhanced in the face of complex data and multi-source information input. This study opens up new paths and strategies for future research on multimodal AI in the field of privacy protection.
